LAST_SUCCESS=RESOLVED+VERIFIED: eleev-2048 AttributeGraph UAF fixed at the root (Compute 2e3ed43, pushed to wasm32-wasip1). Two real defects: (1) Graph::remove_subgraph missing an erase from _invalidating_subgraphs (stale queue entry -> invalidate_now on freed/reused memory tears down an unrelated live subgraph); (2) table::alloc_page multi-page scan control-flow bug (unconditional `found=true` after a mid-scan conflict hands an already-in-use page to a second zone). Deterministic headless repro (WandrHeadless.swift, #if WANDR_HEADLESS) went from 100% crash-at-round-0 to 6/6 clean 60/60-round runs. Confirmed on the real app on both Linux and Windows hosts by the user.
NOTES=Full derivation: swift/OpenSwiftUIProject/tests/oag-baseline/CROSS-LINKED-PAGE-CHAIN-FINDINGS.md + memory reference_openswiftui_headless_uaf_repro.md. Diagnostic-only instrumentation (page-owner map, free-history, live-subgraph registry, WANDR_IMMORTAL_GRAPH bisection flag) was removed after the fix landed; kept permanently: the two fixes + one cheap contains_subgraph() regression guard in Graph::invalidate_subgraphs(). The #if WANDR_HEADLESS repro stays as reusable regression infra (build via repros/swift-canvas-spike/build-headless.sh). eleev/swiftui-2048 source remains unmodified except one real latent bug fix (AboutView.swift force-unwrapped URL(string:"") when the Strings plist/assets are absent).
